[x] Expose the workspace to Claude Code =claude-code-interface $Completed. The Claude Code adapter mirrors Pi's two-organ loop without replacing native tool authority. Organ 1: PostToolUse(Read) forwards the raw read window to kernel-owned observe-read. Organ 2: SessionStart pushes kernel brief status and checkpoint delta. Live cold-session dogfood exposed Claude's bounded hook-output preview (the original 17,282-byte payload hid claim 45 and the checkpoint), so the transport now places a compact preview index first while retaining verbatim kernel status/delta for reveal. Redrive proved the exact objective, checkpoint, and all six active claim freshness rows reached inline model context without tool calls. Acceptance: 16/16 orientation-drive checks plus the existing capture-read drive; no-Git, empty-workspace, malformed-input, and missing-runtime paths remain harmless/silent. Known residual: preview headlines are bounded but claim cardinality is not; if the active set grows past the preview budget, add a kernel-owned bounded wake projection. Deferred separately: repoint Pi capture.ts at observe-read and add a pull-side Claude orientation command.$ !2 +integration ^2026-09-01T22:33 %2026-09-02T10:16 <kernel #01a0609b-d78f-7213-8aa7-7a40ee7f6b8b
[x] Expose the agent-native tool surface through Pi =pi-interface $Completed. The project-local Pi extension preserves native read authority while auto-capturing finalized model-boundary reads through kernel-owned observe-read; duplicate adapter capture planning is deleted. It strips only Pi pagination chrome, streams selected text to kernel stdin, and separately preserves complete model-visible byte accounting. workspace_status and workspace_delta now use compact kernel-bounded defaults with explicit omission counts and full audit expansion. Runtime absence is honest for both no-Git and missing-binary cases. Fresh pi -p dogfood read README.md without Bash/manual kernel use and produced observation 154 (pi.read, whole-file, 5,004 bytes); bounded delta advanced 17→18 while retaining 16 recent ids. Validated by 38 Rust tests, strict fmt/clippy, 4 Pi tests plus typecheck, and the shared Claude drive. Known residuals: later-loaded Pi context middleware can still alter finalized projection; outside-range concurrent edits can affect container provenance; silent fail-closed skips remain intentionally non-disruptive.$ !2 +integration ^2026-08-31T22:31 %2026-09-02T10:54 <kernel #01a05b73-6878-7920-bdd3-e8e37f37b4da
[x] Fix the edit-time hook that reformats Rust files non-canonically $RESOLVED 2026-09-02 (commit d9dc2c2). Root cause was NOT version skew (system rustfmt and pinned toolchain are the same rustfmt 1.9.0) but EDITION: cargo fmt reads edition 2024 from Cargo.toml; pi-lens format-on-edit and LSP formatters invoke a bare 'rustfmt <file>' that never sees Cargo.toml and defaults to edition 2015, which reflows multi-line assert!(...) into a compressed form. Reproduced exactly: 'rustfmt --check tests/walking_skeleton.rs' emits the drift byte-for-byte; '--edition 2024 --check' is clean. Fix: rustfmt.toml (edition = 2024) at repo root; rustfmt discovers it from each input file dir upward, converging cargo fmt + bare rustfmt + LSP + pi-lens on one canonical form. Verified a bare in-repo rustfmt rewrite now leaves files identical and cargo fmt stays clean. Residuals: (a) unverified against a live pi-lens run — bare-rustfmt is a faithful proxy, confirm next Pi session; (b) TypeScript .ts sources (run-9) NOT covered by this Rust-only fix; open a new action if pi-lens prettier/biome drift on .ts recurs.$ !5 +environment ^2026-09-01T19:18 %2026-09-02T11:42 #01a05fe9-40b4-7880-b405-ce1fbc0d8820
[x] Implement semantic locations and bounded working sets =working-set $COMPLETED 2026-09-02 (commits e57f28d kernel, e9c349e Pi). New 'working-set' command projects focused observations into a bounded, restart-safe attention model. All 7 acceptance criteria met: (1) uncited surfacing = current observations no active claim supports and not focused; (2) focus+reason already existed; (3) semantic location is a PROJECTION joining working-set entry -> observation (path/selector/revision/relocation-fingerprint) — not a stored entity, one source of truth; (4) three hard-bounded sections (locations cap 12 stale-first-then-recency, uncited cap 12, trail cap 16) each with explicit _omitted count, no whole-file payload retained; (5) freshness joined from reconciled observations, edited location goes stale and sorts first; (6) navigation trail + working set both replayed from ObservationFocused event order, no event-schema change (focus_sequence derived), recover on restart — verified on the live 172-obs/16-focus log with no migration; (7) parameterless workspace_working_set Pi tool mirrors workspace_status/delta. Coverage: 2 Rust acceptance tests (40 total), 5 Pi tests + typecheck, strict fmt/clippy. See docs/implementation-notes.md 2026-09-02 sections.$ !1 +implementation ^2026-08-31T22:31 %2026-09-02T11:44 <kernel #01a05b73-6855-7791-83e4-0e7b6fcf9bb1
[x] Implement findings and validation evidence =findings $COMPLETED 2026-09-02 (commits 87be10c A, 273abe8 B+C). Findings = a persistent quickfix-like queue of provider-reported issues, distinct from the pre-existing Evidence. KEY DESIGN: freshness (current/stale/unknown, from reconcile) kept ORTHOGONAL to disposition (open/resolved/deferred/suppressed/false-positive, each with actor+rationale, invariant 8) — diverging from initial-design.md which folded stale into one lifecycle enum, mirroring the claim-vs-supersession split. A finding binds to one location and reconciles freshness via the shared location_freshness_verdict extracted from observation reconcile (they cannot drift). Native payload = the provider's own raw output (supplied on stdin, retained in CAS keyed by its own digest, verified on reveal, fail-closed), distinct from the source file which is only the freshness binding (S8). Surface: record-finding, reveal-finding, dispose-finding, findings (bounded queue ranked most-severe-first, cap 12, omission count, freshness histogram, disposed count), plus status open_findings count and a workspace_findings Pi tool. Coverage: 3 Rust acceptance tests (43 total) + 1 Pi test (6 total) + typecheck, strict fmt/clippy. See docs/implementation-notes.md 2026-09-02 findings sections.$ !1 +implementation ^2026-08-31T22:31 %2026-09-02T12:19 <working-set #01a05b73-6862-7411-adb5-bd229ccaa248
[x] Implement reversible change transactions =transactions $COMPLETED 2026-09-02 (commit f352776). AUDIT first: begin/apply/revert and accept (accept is BOTH validate and commit — accepts only when every acceptance claim is current with current passing evidence) already existed (S6/S9/S10). This slice added the charter's association layer: (1) intent required at begin (Transaction.intent); (2) associate-finding links addressed findings (association only, idempotent, open-only) and record-risk records residual risks, via new events; (3) preview-transaction — a pure WorkspaceStatus::transaction_preview projecting intent, affected locations (distinct mutation paths), associated findings w/ freshness, bearing evidence, acceptance claims, residual risks, and ready_to_accept+reason via acceptance_readiness (same rule accept enforces, read-only; a test drives both directions so preview can't drift from accept); plus a workspace_transaction_preview Pi tool. DEFERRED as charter non-goals: changed-symbol identity and dependency-level blast radius (need the symbol model the charter declines to over-invest in) — affected-locations=mutation-paths is the derivable version. 44 Rust + 7 Pi tests. See docs/implementation-notes.md 2026-09-02 transactions section.$ !1 +implementation ^2026-08-31T22:31 %2026-09-02T13:16 <findings #01a05b73-686d-7523-a4d4-b5c4c7d741f9
